(Bug #66's guard: giving a function body every global's declared type must
 not out-rank the names the function binds itself. LANGUAGE.md:711 - "Declaring
 a variable inside a function shadows a top-level variable of the same name" -
 and a parameter is the same story. Both are declared here against globals
 that sit BELOW the functions, and of a different type, so a seeded global
 type would be visible in the wrong place if it won.)

